 abstract = {This research illustrates how risk domain moderates the effects of
priming the interdependent self versus the independent self on
consumers' risk-taking. Experiment 1 showed that individuals whose
interdependent selves were activated were more risk-seeking in their
financial choices and less risk-seeking in their social choices than
