@article{WOS:000307464400010,
 abstract = {The potential of social media has expanded far beyond the initial
function of social communication among a network of friends. It has
become an increasingly important tool in risk communication to allow the
dissemination of timely and accurate information to global citizens to
make more informed choices regarding a particular crisis. The Fukushima
nuclear crisis is an example where the potential of social media was not
fully tapped. This caused undue stress and distrust of authorities.
While the use of social media in this crisis could have altered
significantly the level of trust in authorities and others, two
additional points should be considered. One point is the use of plain
language versus scientific language in order to reach a wider audience.
The other is an urgent need to improve public information especially in
the event of a nuclear emergency and to enhance educational efforts and
action by improving radiological protection communication from
regulatory bodies and international agencies. These are points that also
play a large role in the use of social media. Health Phys.
