@article{WOS:000440325900013,
 abstract = {There are various types of elder abuse; one of the most prevalent and
most harmful abuses is neglect. Social isolation is one of the most
common consequences of neglect, with an inability to find meaning in
life dosely associated with both these issues. One intervention that
might be used with older people suffering from neglect and social
isolation is Logotherapy-a meaning-based intervention. The aim of this
study is to examine the effectiveness of Logotherapy in mitigating the
social isolation of older people suffering from neglect. This study was
developed using a quantitative research design, and with a purposive
sample of forty-three socially isolated older individuals in a single
institution for the elderly in Cairo, Egypt. The study follows a
quasi-experimental study model. A social disconnectedness scale and a
perceived isolation scale were used to assess both degrees of social
isolation. The intervention lasted for twelve weeks, with two weeks of
follow-up work. A significant difference emerged between the
intervention and control groups. The results indicate that enabling
older people to experience meaning in life by emphasising the value of
social relationships and interactions has a positive effect on their
social networks.},
