@article{WOS:000755200100007,
 abstract = {Influence Maximization (IM) is the problem of finding k influential
nodes in a network to increase the spread or influence of a specific
matter. It has been an amazing topic through recent years. Later studies
proposed algorithms and heuristics to either accelerate seed selection
process or introduce new diffusion models. Two of important aspects in
diffusion are trust and time. There have been several studies in either
aspect, but to our best knowledge there is a great lack in considering
both time and trust together in articles. Still one other important
problem is the propagation of negative ideas. It is obvious that we
cannot neglect this type of effects and must find a way to reduce it or
``USE{''} it in a wise way. We chose to use this effect against their
selves and maximize the positive effect. In addition, we considered time
constraint to better sculpt the real world in our diffusion model. We
used a greedy based framework to select seed nodes. By utilizing an
approximation for marginal influence, the seed selection process is
accelerated. Comparing with other related methods, results show the
superiority of our proposed method while dealing with two important and
complex matters.},
