@article{WOS:000984031200001,
 abstract = {Megaproject governance is a new way to enhance risk prevention and
control and improve project performance. However, how to deal with the
dilemma of incomplete megaproject governance mechanism and the unclear
relationship between elements, and promote the coordination of
governance objectives and governance paths, has become a pressing
challenge in the process of risk prevention and control of megaproject
projects. This study constructs a relational network model of a
mega-project governance mechanism based on risk prevention and control
by using the social network analysis method. The position and influence
of core elements in the relational network are explored, and the
relationships between network structures are analysed. It has been shown
that risk communication, government coordination, benefit distribution,
commitment and risk sharing are at the centre of the relational network
of megaproject governance mechanisms. Risk communication and government
coordination are key nodes in a relational network of elements that play
an important role in the effectiveness of project governance and are
closely connected to other elements in the relational network.},
