@article{WOS:001181776500001,
 abstract = {At present, online reviews played an important role in the governance of
environmental problems. Based on the theory of risk perception, we used
online reviews of the smog from 2014 to 2018 as the data source to
analyze the spatiotemporal difference between PM2.5 concentration and
online reviews. We summarize the correlation mechanism between smog and
online reviews. The conclusions are as follows: (1) From the perspective
of the relationship between smog and online reviews, PM2.5 had a growth
effect on online reviews, while online reviews had a short-term
inhibition effect on PM2.5. (2) Online reviews only inhibited the
concentration of PM2.5 in 2015. Online reviews when are in the peak had
raised the environmental awareness of the Chinese public and the
government's environmental governance efforts. This also indirectly led
to changes in the driving mechanism of PM2.5 concentration after 2015.
(3) Economic density had negative effect on PM2.5 after 2015, which is
consistent with theory of Environmental Kuznets Curve. This study
provided a theoretical reference for the interaction between online
reviews and smog. The government can adjust the environmental protection
strategy according to the risk perception through online reviews.},
