trial, was implemented to test effects of telephone-based psychosocial
interventions delivered by older-adult volunteers for low-income lonely
older adults. To evaluate the effects of volunteering on loneliness, we
randomized 375 individuals ages 50-70 into a volunteering condition
versus an active control (psychoeducation with social gatherings).
Following a 6-week training, participants in the volunteering condition,
delivered tele-interventions to older intervention recipients.
